{"object":"USB-C identifies connector form, while protocol, Power Delivery, alternate modes, cable capability, and performance are separate. A connector label alone therefore cannot establish that an old charger supplies the required protocol or wattage to either phone.","predicate":"distinguishes","source_url":"http://localhost:8090/content/wikipedia_en_all_nopic/USB-C","subject":"USB-C capability boundary","text":"USB-C is a connector form rather than a guarantee of USB Power Delivery, alternate modes, cable capability, wattage or performance. The old charger and cable must be inspected instead of inferring compatibility from connector shape.","title":"prop_usb_c_capability_scope"}